{"id":"bw-dwe","title":"Add sort-by-priority toggle to kanban board columns","description":"Add a sort order toggle on the Board page that lets users switch between 'Date' (current default, newest first) and 'Priority' (P0 first) sorting for kanban columns. Persist choice to localStorage. KanbanBoard needs a sortOrder prop, BoardPage needs a toggle button.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-24T23:39:13Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-24T23:40:36Z","closed_at":"2026-02-24T23:40:36Z","close_reason":"Added sort toggle button to Board page header. Toggles between Date (newest first) and Priority (P0 first) sorting for all kanban columns. Choice persisted to localStorage.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-19m","title":"Wire up epic filter dropdown on Board page and include epic in results","description":"The epic filter dropdown already exists in FilterBar but BoardPage never passes availableEpics so it's hidden. Fix: (1) extract epics from allIssues and pass to FilterBar, (2) update applyFilter so epic filter shows the epic itself plus its children, not just children.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-24T21:17:05Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:20:36Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:20:36Z","close_reason":"Already implemented — availableParents map passed to FilterBar, applyFilter shows epic + children","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-7t5","title":"Add date range filter to FilterBar on Board page","description":"Add a date range filter to FilterBar allowing users to filter issues by created_at date. Add createdAfter/createdBefore fields to FilterCriteria, implement in applyFilter(), and add date picker UI to FilterBar. Also implement the existing isStale/isRecent criteria that are declared but unimplemented.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-24T19:39:09Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-24T19:46:05Z","closed_at":"2026-02-24T19:46:05Z","close_reason":"Added createdAfter/createdBefore to FilterCriteria, implemented in applyFilter with date range logic, added DateRangeFilter dropdown to FilterBar, implemented isStale/isRecent, added Recent and Stale built-in views, 4 new tests","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-7t5","depends_on_id":"bw-8uc","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-24T19:39:15Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-7t5","depends_on_id":"bw-e8l","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-24T19:39:14Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-8uc","title":"Display created_at date on FleetCard component","description":"Show the created_at date on FleetCard for the Fleet board. The epic's created_at is available via FleetApp.epic. Display as relative time or short date.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-24T19:39:09Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-24T19:43:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-24T19:43:02Z","close_reason":"Added formatRelativeDate helper and date display to FleetCard header","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-e8l","title":"Display created_at date on IssueCard component","description":"Show the created_at date on both card and row variants of IssueCard. The data already exists on PlanIssue but is not rendered. Display as a relative time (e.g. '3d ago') or short date format. Both variants (kanban card and table row) should show it.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-24T18:54:22Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-24T19:43:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-24T19:43:02Z","close_reason":"Added formatRelativeDate helper and date display to both card and row variants of IssueCard","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-7yt","title":"Closed PatchCycle issues show as open in projects_master view","description":"Issues closed in PatchCycle beads (e.g. PatchCycle-9m2) show correctly as closed when selecting PatchCycle from the beads-web dropdown, but show as open when selecting projects_master. bd sync has been run and makes no difference. Root cause is likely stale data in the projects_master hub.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T01:27:56Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T01:36:03Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T01:36:03Z","close_reason":"Root cause: sync-hub.sh used --skip-existing on import so status changes never propagated, and it read from main .beads/issues.jsonl which was stale (bd sync writes to worktree JSONL). Fixed by: (1) adding worktree-aware JSONL resolution, (2) adding a status-update step that syncs status/priority/closed_at from source repos to hub by title match.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
