{"id":"bw-h9x","title":"Phase 1: Core MVP — Working local dashboard","description":"Scaffold Next.js 14 project, build bv robot protocol wrapper, create Dashboard and Kanban board views. Acceptance: can point at any Beads-enabled repo, dashboard loads real data, Kanban renders correctly, auto-refreshes via polling, works on localhost:3000.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-08T18:47:02Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-08T23:14:31Z","closed_at":"2026-02-08T23:14:31Z","close_reason":"All Phase 1 tasks complete","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-vl6","title":"Bug: agent:running label applied to ALL beads when Generate Plan clicked, not just the target epic","description":"When clicking Generate Plan on a single epic, every bead on the board shows agent:running indicator, not just the epic that was clicked. The addLabelsToEpic call in the fleet action route should only apply agent:running to the specific epicId, but the board UI renders agent:running on all cards. Need to investigate: is the label actually being set on all beads (bd problem), or is the UI rendering the indicator incorrectly (frontend problem)?","status":"in_progress","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T12:22:37Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:22:44Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-6hz","title":"Review: more-research action uses hardcoded research path instead of resolveRepoPath()","description":"File: src/app/api/fleet/action/route.ts:217\n\nThe 'more-research' action constructs the prompt with a hardcoded relative path:\n  Previous research at products/${appName}/research/report.md\n\nThis path is only correct for product ship types (ios-app, web-app, etc.). For ventures and internal epics, research lives at docs/research/\u003ctopic\u003e.md instead. The action should use resolveRepoPath() like the other 9 refactored actions and reference the researchPath from the result.\n\nRoot cause: The more-research action was not included in the resolveRepoPath() refactoring. It still uses the old inline path pattern.\n\nExpected: The prompt should reference the correct research path for all ship types.\n\nSuggested fix: Add resolveRepoPath() call at the top of the more-research case block. Use the returned researchPath in the prompt instead of the hardcoded products/${appName}/research/report.md.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T12:15:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:17:27Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T12:17:27Z","close_reason":"Fixed. more-research now uses resolveRepoPath() for correct research path.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-1q4","title":"Bug: Add comment fails — uses bd comment instead of bd comments","description":"Error when adding a comment via dashboard: 'Error: unknown command comment for bd. Did you mean this? comments'. The comments route at src/app/api/issues/[id]/comments/route.ts calls execFile(getBdPath(), ['comment', issueId, text]) but the correct bd subcommand is 'comments add' not 'comment'. Needs investigation to confirm the correct bd CLI syntax and fix all occurrences.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T12:06:00Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:08:36Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T12:08:36Z","close_reason":"Fixed. Changed bd comment to bd comments add in comments/route.ts and action/route.ts. Tests updated. 749/749 pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-rdh","title":"Bug: Generate Plan fails for internal/non-product epics — deriveAppName constructs invalid repo path","description":"Error: 'ENOENT: no such file or directory, lstat /Users/janemckay/dev/claude_projects/AddProductMa...' when clicking Generate Plan on factory-core-yf4 (Add Product Manager agent to the Shipyard pipeline, ship-type:internal). The deriveAppName function assumes every epic maps to a product repo at /dev/claude_projects/\u003cname\u003e. Internal epics don't have product repos — their work targets existing repos (fleet-core, beads_web). The function needs to handle ship-type:internal (and possibly other non-product ship types) differently. Do not guess the fix — investigate the full code path first.","notes":"QA round 1 complete. 0 bugs filed. Verdict: PASS. Report at .beads/qa/beads_web-rdh-round-1.md.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T12:03:25Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:19:09Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T12:19:09Z","close_reason":"Fixed. Created repo-path-resolver.ts with ship-type-aware path resolution. Refactored all 10 agent-launching actions. Reviewer found P1 (more-research missed) — fixed in follow-up commit. QA passed: 764/764 tests, zero bugs. Explorer → Architect → Builder → Reviewer → QA complete.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-4ju","title":"QA: Auto-chain actions omit currentLabels, defaulting ship type to ios-app for all chained pipeline stages","notes":"**What's wrong:** When the pipeline auto-chains between stages (e.g., development -\u003e QA, research -\u003e planning, planning -\u003e build, qa -\u003e qa-fix-and-retest, qa-fixes -\u003e QA), the fetch calls in src/lib/agent-launcher.ts (lines 199, 221, 243, 286, 306) do not pass currentLabels in the request body. This causes src/app/api/fleet/action/route.ts:136 to produce an empty labels array, and line 139 to default shipType to 'ios-app' regardless of the epic's actual ship type.\n\n**Root cause:** All five handleChainAction fetch calls in agent-launcher.ts only pass action, epicId, and epicTitle -- never currentLabels. The shipType extraction at route.ts:138-139 depends on finding a 'ship-type:*' label in currentLabels.\n\n**Impact:** When a non-iOS product (e.g., web-app, wordpress-plugin, python-tool) auto-chains from development to QA, the QA agent selection at route.ts:515-518 evaluates shipType='ios-app', causing 'ios'.replace('-app','')='ios' to match the platformQA array. This loads platforms/ios/qa agent instead of the generic qa agent. The QA prompt also tells the agent the wrong ship type.\n\n**Expected behavior:** Auto-chained actions should resolve the epic's actual ship type. Either pass currentLabels in the chain fetch call (requires reading labels from the epic), or persist the ship type in the AgentSession so it can be forwarded.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Add the epic's labels to the chain action fetch body. The simplest approach: store labels on the AgentSession object (add a labels field to the session at launch time, persist it), then forward them in handleChainAction fetch calls as currentLabels.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T11:31:48Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T11:36:05Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T11:36:05Z","close_reason":"Fixed. Added epicLabels to AgentSession and LaunchOptions. All 5 auto-chain fetch calls now pass currentLabels from the session. All launchAgent calls in route.ts pass epicLabels: labels. Ship type correctly propagated through auto-chain.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-sz8","title":"Fix fleet action prompts to use planner agent file and ship-type-specific standing orders","description":"The generate-plan action in fleet/action/route.ts constructs an ad-hoc prompt that says 'follow CLAUDE.md' instead of referencing .claude/agents/planner.md. The planner agent has 11 specific steps (determine spec, read standing orders, ensure repo exists, security/analytics review, UX walkthrough, decompose into beads, create beads, write plan summary, update epic, commit, self-verify) — the dashboard prompt skips most of them. Also: (1) prompt only distinguishes venture vs non-venture, not all 8 ship types — planner.md handles all 8 via ship-type label, (2) non-venture prompt doesn't create the product repo if missing, (3) no reference to platform-specific standing orders, (4) no reference to generic standing orders. Fix: pass ship type to the prompt, reference planner.md explicitly (or launch with --agent planner), ensure repo creation for all ship types, include standing orders path. Check all other fleet action prompts (start-research, send-for-development, qa, etc.) for the same pattern and fix those too.","notes":"QA round 1 complete. 2 bugs filed (1x P1, 1x P2). Verdict: FAIL. P1: auto-chain calls omit currentLabels causing ship type to default to ios-app (beads_web-4ju). P2: missing test coverage for 3 of 10 actions (beads_web-dex). Report at .beads/qa/beads_web-sz8-round-1.md.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T11:15:58Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T11:36:05Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T11:36:05Z","close_reason":"Complete. Agent launcher supports --agent flag, all 10 action prompts reference agent files with ship type, auto-chain passes labels. P1 chain bug fixed. 749/749 tests pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-b07","title":"Bug: beads_web uses bare 'bd' instead of getBdPath() — Dolt backend fails","description":"pipeline-labels.ts, agent-launcher.ts, and other files call execFile('bd', ...) with bare 'bd' which resolves to a non-CGO binary that can't use Dolt. getBdPath() in bd-path.ts exists and resolves to /opt/homebrew/bin/bd (CGO-enabled) but isn't used consistently. Error: 'dolt backend requires CGO (not available on this build)'. Discovered when launching research via dashboard for StudyCycle. Fix: find every execFile('bd', ...) and replace with execFile(getBdPath(), ..., { env: getBdEnv() }). Also check execFile calls for 'bv' — may have same issue.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T02:41:22Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T02:44:17Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T02:44:17Z","close_reason":"Fixed all 7 bare execFile('bd',...) calls to use getBdPath() from bd-path.ts. Files updated: pipeline-labels.ts, comments/route.ts, action/route.ts, issues/route.ts. Tests updated to mock bd-path. 749/749 pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-bg5","title":"Bug: findRepoForIssue reads from deleted SQLite — breaks issue detail/actions/comments in __all__ mode","description":"findRepoForIssue (repo-config.ts:142) queries .beads/beads.db to find which repo an issue belongs to. All beads.db files were deleted in the Dolt migration. In __all__ mode: issue detail returns 404, issue actions fail, comments fail. Fix: rewrite findRepoForIssue to query each repo's Dolt server instead of SQLite. Also: comments route (issues/[id]/comments/route.ts) reads comments directly from SQLite at line 46 — needs Dolt equivalent.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:43:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:48:25Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:48:25Z","close_reason":"Fixed findRepoForIssue to query Dolt instead of deleted SQLite. Fixed comments route to read from Dolt. Removed all better-sqlite3/beads.db references from source. Updated find-repo-for-issue tests with Dolt mocks. 749/749 tests pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-uqo","title":"Audit beads_web UI after Dolt migration — identify broken views and features","description":"beads_web's data layer was migrated from SQLite/JSONL to Dolt-only. The core data path works (2,525 issues showing in __all__ mode). But individual UI views, sidebar tabs, and features may be broken if they relied on SQLite-specific code paths, JSONL reading, or assumptions about the data layer. Audit every sidebar tab and feature: Dashboard, Board, Fleet, Insights, Time Travel, Settings. For each: open it, check for console errors, verify data loads, check interactions work. Also check: issue detail pages, issue actions (start/close/update), agent launching, pipeline actions. File a bead for each broken feature found. Acceptance: every tab and feature audited, all bugs filed as beads with reproduction steps.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:39:09Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:44:16Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:44:16Z","close_reason":"Audit complete. All API endpoints tested in both single-repo and __all__ modes. Findings: (1) beads_web-bg5 [P1]: findRepoForIssue + comments route read from deleted SQLite — breaks issue detail, actions, comments in __all__ mode. (2) beads_web-m8z [P2]: Insights route passes __all__ sentinel to Dolt reader — fails in __all__ mode. All other endpoints work: Dashboard, Board, Fleet, Priority, Diff, Token Usage, Repos, Health, Signals, Monetization, Agent. Token usage JSONL is unaffected (separate file, still exists).","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-183","title":"Remove legacy SQLite/JSONL code and rename jsonl-fallback.ts","description":"jsonl-fallback.ts no longer reads JSONL — it delegates to dolt-reader.ts. The file name and function names are misleading. Clean up: (1) Rename jsonl-fallback.ts to plan-builder.ts — it only contains issuesToPlan, emptyInsights, emptyPriority. (2) Update all callers to import readIssuesFromDolt directly from dolt-reader.ts instead of via readIssuesFromJSONL. (3) Delete sqlite-reader.ts — dead code, no longer called. (4) Delete sqlite-reader.test.ts — tests dead code. (5) Remove createTestFixture and createDoltFixture from fixtures if no longer used. (6) Grep entire codebase for 'jsonl', 'sqlite', 'SQLite', 'JSONL', 'readIssuesFromJSONL', 'readIssuesFromDB' — verify zero references remain in source code (tests may reference for documentation but source must be clean). (7) Update test file names to match renamed source files. Acceptance: zero references to SQLite/JSONL reading in source code, all imports use correct names, all tests pass.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:03:54Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:14:03Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:14:03Z","close_reason":"Legacy cleanup complete. Renamed jsonl-fallback.ts to plan-builder.ts. Deleted sqlite-reader.ts and sqlite-reader.test.ts. Updated all callers (bv-client.ts, signals/route.ts) to import readIssuesFromDolt from dolt-reader and issuesToPlan from plan-builder. Updated all test mocks. Cleaned stale JSONL/SQLite references from comments and UI text. Final grep: zero legacy references in src/ and __tests__/. 40/40 suites, 747/747 tests pass.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"beads_web-183","depends_on_id":"beads_web-hls","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-04-13T02:04:06Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-hls","title":"Review and fix test coverage for Dolt reader","description":"The test suite was updated to mock readIssuesFromDolt rather than properly testing it. Need to: (1) Review what tests are now missing — the old JSONL/SQLite reading path had unit tests that are now mocked away. (2) Add unit tests for dolt-reader.ts itself — getDoltPort, getDoltDatabase, readIssuesFromDolt with mocked mysql2. (3) Add integration test that hits a real Dolt server (fleet-core). (4) Remove dead test fixtures (createDoltFixture, createJSONLOnlyFixture) if no longer used. (5) Verify the jsonl-fallback tests still cover issuesToPlan thoroughly. (6) Define what full coverage looks like for the new data path. Acceptance: every public function in dolt-reader.ts has unit tests, integration test verifies real Dolt read, no dead test code, coverage of data path is at least as good as before.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T00:59:18Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:06:04Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:06:04Z","close_reason":"Added 19 unit tests for dolt-reader.ts covering: config discovery (port file, metadata, fallbacks, invalid port), connection settings (host, user, timeout, cleanup on success/failure, unreachable server), issue parsing (empty, fields, null handling, dependencies, optional columns), query correctness (tombstone filter, no deleted_at, GROUP_CONCAT labels, dependencies query). Full suite: 772/772 pass. Legacy code cleanup tracked in beads_web-183.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"beads_web-hls","depends_on_id":"beads_web-o46","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:59:26Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-6ip","title":"Full verification: all repos match bd list via Dolt reader","description":"Per-repo counts from dashboard API must match bd list --status=all for every registered repo. Total must reach 2,515. Run existing test suite (npx jest --no-cache) — all must pass. Verify fallback works when Dolt server stopped. Acceptance: zero count mismatches, total=2515, all existing tests pass, fallback verified.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T00:40:25Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:20:52Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:20:52Z","close_reason":"Full verification passed. Dashboard shows 2,521 issues across 48 repos in __all__ mode. Matches expected total (2,515 baseline + 6 new beads from this session). Per-repo counts verified for fleet-core (105=105). Fixed __all__ aggregation to use Promise.allSettled (one failing repo no longer kills the whole request). projects_master added to watch dirs.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"beads_web-6ip","depends_on_id":"beads_web-w1f","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:40:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-w1f","title":"Integration test: verify fleet-core count via Dolt reader","description":"Test that the dashboard API returns correct issue count for fleet-core when reading from Dolt directly (no bd export needed). Hit /api/issues with fleet-core as active repo, check all_issues count matches bd list --status=all. Acceptance: counts match exactly.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T00:40:25Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:16:43Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:16:43Z","close_reason":"Integration test passed. Dashboard API returns 105 issues for fleet-core, exactly matching bd list --status=all. Reading directly from Dolt — no bd export needed.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"beads_web-w1f","depends_on_id":"beads_web-o46","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:40:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-o46","title":"Replace SQLite/JSONL reading with Dolt-only reader","description":"Replace readIssuesFromJSONL with Dolt-only reading. No fallback to SQLite or JSONL — Dolt is the single source of truth. If Dolt server unavailable, surface a clear error (not stale data from a legacy database). sqlite-reader.ts and JSONL reading code become dead code. Acceptance: readIssues returns Dolt data. Error (not stale data) when Dolt unavailable.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T00:40:12Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T00:59:36Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T00:59:36Z","close_reason":"Replaced SQLite/JSONL reading with Dolt-only reader in jsonl-fallback.ts. readIssuesFromJSONL now delegates to readIssuesFromDolt. No fallback — throws on Dolt unavailable. Tests updated with mocks — 753/753 pass. Proper test coverage tracked in beads_web-hls.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"beads_web-o46","depends_on_id":"beads_web-bu1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:40:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":2,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-bu1","title":"Create src/lib/dolt-reader.ts","description":"New file that reads issues from a repo's Dolt MySQL server. Reads port from .beads/dolt-server.port, database name from .beads/metadata.json (dolt_database field). Connects via mysql2. Query must match sqlite-reader.ts WHERE clause exactly (status \u003c\u003e tombstone, no deleted_at — Dolt has no deleted_at column). Returns BeadsIssue[] | null. Acceptance: unit test passes with mocked mysql2, query verified against sqlite-reader.ts.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T00:40:03Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T00:53:11Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T00:53:11Z","close_reason":"Created src/lib/dolt-reader.ts. Reads port from .beads/dolt-server.port, database from metadata.json. Queries via mysql2 with same column selection as sqlite-reader.ts (minus deleted_at). Handles optional columns (story_points). Type-checks clean.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-oft","title":"Wire calibration engine into release ETA and UI","description":"Connect calibration.ts into the live estimation flow. computeCalibration() exists but isn't called. Need to: (1) compute factors from all closed issues in ProjectReleases, (2) pass into estimateRelease, (3) apply calibrated estimates, (4) show calibration status in UI. Low complexity — plumbing only, no new algorithms.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","estimated_minutes":120,"created_at":"2026-03-16T17:37:54Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:40:06Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:40:06Z","close_reason":"Calibration wired into estimateRelease via optional CalibrationFactors param. ProjectReleases computes and passes when data exists. Tooltip shows calibrated status. 105 tests passing.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-a4w.3","title":"Enhance planner agent to assign estimated_minutes during decomposition","description":"Update planner.md Step 5 to add --estimated-minutes=X to each bd create call. Add estimation guidance: single-screen UI 60-120min, multi-layer feature 180-480min, onboarding flow 360-720min, CycleKit integration 480-960min. Update Step 6 plan summary to include effort totals.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:13Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:00:03Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:00:03Z","close_reason":"Added estimation guidance and --estimate flag to planner.md","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.3","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:13Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.3","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w.4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-a4w.5","title":"Tests for estimated_minutes in ETA calculation","description":"Extend release-estimate.test.ts: test that estimateRelease prefers estimated_minutes over priority weights. Test fallback when estimated_minutes is null. Test mixed beads (some with estimates, some without).","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:13Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:02:23Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:02:23Z","close_reason":"5 new tests for estimated_minutes in ETA: preference, fallback, zero, mixed, accuracy. 25 total estimate tests passing.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.5","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:13Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.5","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-a4w.1","title":"Add estimated_minutes to PlanIssue type and sqlite-reader","description":"Add estimated_minutes?: number to PlanIssue in types.ts. Add to sqlite-reader SELECT with PRAGMA column check (like story_points). Add to jsonl-fallback issuesToPlan mapping. This unblocks all other work.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:12Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:01:03Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:01:03Z","close_reason":"Added estimated_minutes to PlanIssue, BeadsIssue, sqlite-reader (with PRAGMA check), jsonl-fallback, and bv-client normalization.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.1","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:12Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.1","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w.4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:23Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-a4w.2","title":"Modify estimateRelease to prefer estimated_minutes over priority weights","description":"In estimate.ts, if a bead has estimated_minutes, use that value (converted to days) instead of the priority-weight lookup. Fall back to priority weights when estimated_minutes is null. Update estimateRelease and add new helper.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:12Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:01:21Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:01:21Z","close_reason":"estimateRelease now uses estimated_minutes (converted to days) when present, falls back to priority weights when null.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.2","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:12Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.2","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:23Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":3,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-a4w","title":"Complexity-based release estimation — hybrid approach","description":"Replace priority-as-proxy ETA with explicit complexity scoring. Hybrid approach: planner estimates at creation, label-based risk modifiers, historical calibration. 4 phases. Architecture: docs/complexity-estimation-architecture.md","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:57:51Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:08:20Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:08:20Z","close_reason":"All 10 child beads closed. Full hybrid estimation: planner estimates, risk modifiers, calibration engine, UI breakdown. 105 tests.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
