{"id":"bw-q6f","title":"Release overview page: per-project release summary with status","description":"New page/section showing all releases for a project, grouped by release:* label, sorted by version descending. Each release row shows: version, release-status (planning/in-progress/in-review/live), count of beads (open/closed), progress bar. Clicking a release filters to its beads. Shows release lifecycle at a glance. Related factory epic: cycle-apps-factory-nm1.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-08T15:47:30Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-09T00:00:51Z","closed_at":"2026-03-09T00:00:51Z","close_reason":"Release overview page at /releases with per-project grouping","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-ug9","title":"Release filter: filter beads by release:* label on project view","description":"Add a filter/dropdown to the project issues view that reads all distinct release:* labels from the project's beads and lets the user filter by release version. Shows 'All releases' by default. When filtered, only beads with that release:* label are shown. Related factory epic: cycle-apps-factory-nm1.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-08T15:47:29Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-09T00:00:50Z","closed_at":"2026-03-09T00:00:50Z","close_reason":"Release filter dropdown added to FilterBar","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-8jr","title":"Hydration error on /board: sort button server/client mismatch","description":"loadSortOrder() reads localStorage during useState initialization in board/page.tsx:25. Server returns 'date' (window undefined), client returns stored 'priority'. Fix: defer localStorage read to useEffect after hydration.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-25T20:59:35Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-25T21:00:08Z","closed_at":"2026-02-25T21:00:08Z","close_reason":"Fixed: defer localStorage read to useEffect to avoid server/client hydration mismatch","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9.10","title":"Add plan sub-label button logic for Research Complete stage","description":"Core planning gate implementation in beads-web. Update FleetCard.tsx and route.ts to handle plan:pending and plan:approved sub-labels within the Research Complete stage. (1) New action types: generate-plan, approve-plan, revise-plan-from-research. (2) FleetCard button logic at research-complete stage: when NO plan label → show 'Generate Plan', 'More Research', 'Abandon'; when plan:pending → show 'Approve Plan', 'Revise Plan', 'Abandon'; when plan:approved → show 'Start Building', 'Revise Plan', 'Abandon'. (3) route.ts handlers: generate-plan adds plan:pending + agent:running and launches planning agent; approve-plan adds plan:approved and removes plan:pending; revise-plan-from-research re-launches planning agent with feedback. (4) Issue detail page buttons should match. Corresponds to cycle-apps-factory-bv7.5.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:29Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:17Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:17Z","close_reason":"Already implemented — FleetCard has full plan sub-label button logic and route.ts has all handlers","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.10","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:29Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":2,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9.9","title":"Add revise-plan action: Prepare for Launch back to planning","description":"Add a 'Revise Plan' button on fleet cards at the Prepare for Launch (submission-prep) stage. Requires: (1) new 'revise-plan' action type in usePipelineAction.ts and PipelineAction in route.ts, (2) new case in route.ts POST handler that removes pipeline:submission-prep, sets pipeline:research-complete + plan:pending + agent:running, launches planning agent with Jane's feedback from epic notes, (3) new button in FleetCard.tsx at the submission-prep stage alongside 'Launch' and 'Send Back', (4) same button on issue detail page. Corresponds to cycle-apps-factory-bv7.8.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:04Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:28Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:28Z","close_reason":"Already implemented — revise-plan-from-launch button on submission-prep stage and handler in route.ts","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.9","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:04Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.9","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9.10","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:35Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9.8","title":"Add skip-to-plan action: Candidates to plan phase directly","description":"Add a 'Skip to Plan' button on fleet cards at the Candidates stage. Requires: (1) new 'skip-to-plan' action type in usePipelineAction.ts and PipelineAction in route.ts, (2) new case in route.ts POST handler that sets pipeline:research-complete + plan:pending + agent:running, launches planning agent in app repo using epic description as spec (no recon brief), (3) new button in FleetCard.tsx at the idea stage alongside 'Start Research', (4) same button on issue detail page. Corresponds to cycle-apps-factory-bv7.7.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:01Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:28Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:28Z","close_reason":"Already implemented — skip-to-plan button on idea stage and handler in route.ts","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.8","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:01Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.8","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9.10","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:34Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9.3","title":"Add plan section to issue detail page","description":"Update src/app/issue/[id]/page.tsx to show a plan section alongside the existing research report section. Use the issue ID directly to fetch the plan (no app name derivation needed). Show the plan for any issue that has a .beads/plans/\u003cid\u003e.md file — attempt to fetch for all issues and gracefully hide if 404. Render the plan markdown in a collapsible section, similar to the research report. Handle three cases: research only, plan only, both research and plan.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:20Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:39Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:39Z","close_reason":"Plan section already exists in issue detail page","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.3","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:20Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.3","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:26Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9.2","title":"Add usePlanReport hook","description":"Create src/hooks/usePlanReport.ts. Fetches from /api/plan/\u003cissueId\u003e (not app name — plans are keyed by issue ID). Returns { content, repoPath }. Uses TanStack Query with same patterns as useResearchReport (staleTime, placeholderData, enabled guard).","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:16Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:39Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:39Z","close_reason":"Hook already exists at src/hooks/usePlanReport.ts","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.2","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:16Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.2","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:25Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9.1","title":"Add GET /api/plan/[appName] route","description":"Create a new API route at src/app/api/plan/[issueId]/route.ts. Given an issue ID, find which repo it belongs to (search all configured repos), then read .beads/plans/\u003cissueId\u003e.md from that repo. Returns { content: string, repoPath: string } on success, 404 if not found. This is different from the research route which uses app name — plans use issue ID so they work for any issue in any repo.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:15Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:14Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:14Z","close_reason":"Route already existed and is correct","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-0i9.1","depends_on_id":"bw-0i9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:15Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-0i9","title":"Plan viewer: display plan content on issue detail page","description":"Add the ability to view plan documents (.beads/plans/\u003cissue-id\u003e.md) on the issue detail page, alongside existing research report support. Plans are stored per-repo at .beads/plans/\u003cissue-id\u003e.md — this works for ANY issue in ANY repo, not just factory epics. Not all issues will have research — some will only have a plan, some will have both. The API route looks up the issue's repo and reads the plan file by issue ID.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:27:07Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:32Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:18:32Z","close_reason":"All children complete — plan viewer fully implemented","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-b5d","title":"Support multi-repo agent launch","description":"Development agents run in the app folder, not the factory. The agent launch API needs to accept different repoPath values per stage. Research agents run in the factory. Development, submission, and kit agents run in the app repo at /Users/janemckay/dev/claude_projects/\u003cAppName\u003e/. The POST /api/agent endpoint must support specifying the working directory per launch.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:41:04Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","close_reason":"Multi-repo agent launch supported via pipeline-labels module and repo-config lookup for app repos","labels":["agent-launch","pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-lzm","title":"Enable web search in research agent launch","description":"The POST /api/agent call for research must include WebSearch and WebFetch in the allowedTools array. Currently the research agent may not have web access enabled, which limits its ability to do market research, competitor analysis, and pricing research. Verify and fix the allowedTools configuration.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:40:59Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:01Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:01Z","close_reason":"Research agent launch configured with opus model and WebSearch in allowedTools via fleet action API","labels":["agent-launch","pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-tgy","title":"Add development agent launch from beads-web","description":"Send for Development button should call POST /api/agent with the app's repo path (not factory), the development prompt, and appropriate allowed tools. The agent must run IN THE APP FOLDER, create beads issues there, plan, build, and test. The repoPath in the API call must point to /Users/janemckay/dev/claude_projects/\u003cAppName\u003e/, not the factory.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:40:44Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","close_reason":"Development agent launch implemented via POST /api/fleet/action, runs in app repo with maxTurns=500","labels":["agent-launch","pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-63f","title":"Update fleet board columns to match pipeline spec","description":"Current columns: Idea/Research/Development/Submission/Completed. New columns: Ideas, In Research, Research Complete, In Development, Prepare for Submission, Submitted, Kit Management, Bad Ideas. Update the fleet board page to reflect the full pipeline stages. Column mapping driven by stage: labels from the factory repo.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:40:27Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:01Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:01Z","close_reason":"Fleet board updated to 9 pipeline columns with pipeline:* label detection, backward-compatible fallback, and stage-specific config","labels":["pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-fkr","title":"Generic agent launch/stop/status API + fleet UI integration","description":"POST /api/agent/launch spawns claude -p in any configured repo. GET /api/agent/status checks running state. POST /api/agent/stop kills process. Fleet page gets Start Research button.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T21:50:09Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T21:58:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T21:58:15Z","close_reason":"Agent launch API complete: agent-launcher.ts, /api/agent route, useAgent hooks, AgentStatusBanner, Start Research button on fleet cards. 13 tests, all 528 pass, build clean.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-dd0","title":"Restore All Projects aggregation option in web UI","description":"After removing projects_master hub, the All Projects aggregated view option is missing from the web dashboard. Users cannot see a combined view across all repos.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T12:17:53Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T12:19:25Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T12:19:25Z","close_reason":"Added All Projects option to Sidebar RepoSelector dropdown and fixed label to show 'All Projects' when in __all__ mode","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-8lr","title":"Remove hub, read directly from project DBs","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T11:57:38Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T12:25:38Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T12:25:38Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-xsq","title":"Fix OTEL collector: issue_id attribution, cost calculation, model name","description":"The token-usage.jsonl collector is writing records but issue_id is always empty, total_cost_usd is always 0, model is empty, and duration_ms/num_turns are 0. Fix the collector to: (1) resolve issue_id from the active session context, (2) calculate cost based on model pricing, (3) capture model name, (4) track duration and turn counts. Without issue_id, tokens cannot be joined to issues for efficiency metrics.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T17:55:41Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T10:24:01Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T10:24:01Z","close_reason":"Fixed all 5 broken fields in beads-collect-tokens.sh: (1) model: now extracted from .message.model in assistant entries; (2) cost: calculated from token counts x model pricing table; (3) duration_ms: computed from first/last transcript timestamps; (4) num_turns: counted from user-type entries; (5) issue_id: added .current-issue fallback. Also fixed duplicate records by deduplicating on session_id before writing. Backfilled 43 existing records to 3 deduplicated records with correct data. All 347 tests pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-fom","title":"Add token usage display to web dashboard","description":"Add token usage data to the web app UI. Include: per-issue token/cost column in issue list, token usage detail in issue detail view, project-wide token usage summary card on dashboard, token usage over time chart on insights page. Use existing SummaryCard and chart patterns.","notes":"## Checkpoint (2026-02-10)\nCompleted and closed. Implemented: TokenUsageSummary dashboard card, cost column in IssueTable (sortable), per-session token breakdown on issue detail page. Commit 43bb76a, pushed to origin/main. 347 tests pass.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:18:59Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:59:47Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T16:55:58Z","close_reason":"Implemented token usage dashboard UI: summary cards on dashboard, cost column in issue table (sortable), per-session breakdown on issue detail page. 347 tests pass, tsc/lint clean.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-fom","depends_on_id":"bw-co0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-fom","depends_on_id":"bw-dzj","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:34Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-dzj","title":"Add /api/token-usage route to read token-usage.jsonl","description":"New Next.js API route that reads .beads/token-usage.jsonl and returns aggregated token usage data. Support query params: ?issue_id=X for per-issue data, ?summary=true for project-wide aggregation. Return total_tokens, total_cost_usd, breakdown by model, session_count per issue. Follow existing API patterns in src/app/api/.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:18:57Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:41:19Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T16:41:19Z","close_reason":"Built /api/token-usage route with ?summary=true and ?issue_id= params, token-usage.ts reader, useTokenUsage hooks, TokenUsageRecord/IssueTokenSummary types. 26 new tests, all 347 pass.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-dzj","depends_on_id":"bw-co0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-dzj","depends_on_id":"bw-vnu","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:34Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-vnu","title":"Define token-usage.jsonl schema and OTEL-to-file collector","description":"Define the .beads/token-usage.jsonl record format (timestamp, session_id, issue_id, project, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_creation_tokens, cost_usd, model, duration_ms). Build a lightweight collector that reads OTEL console/file output and writes normalized records to .beads/token-usage.jsonl. Include session-to-issue join logic using the session map from the hooks.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:18:54Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:41:18Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T16:41:18Z","close_reason":"Built Stop hook collector (beads-collect-tokens.sh) that parses session transcripts, joins with session-map for issue attribution, writes normalized records to .beads/token-usage.jsonl. Registered in global settings.json.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-vnu","depends_on_id":"bw-co0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-vnu","depends_on_id":"bw-qki","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-qki","title":"Add global OTEL env vars and Claude Code SessionStart hook","description":"Set up the global infrastructure for token tracking. Add CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=1 and OTEL env vars to shell profile template. Create a global Claude Code SessionStart hook (~/.claude/settings.json) that: detects .beads/ in cwd, runs bd list --status=in_progress to get active issue, writes session-to-issue mapping. Also create a PostToolUse hook that watches for bd update --status=in_progress to handle mid-session issue switches.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:18:51Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:27:58Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T16:27:58Z","close_reason":"Implemented and tested. SessionStart hook auto-detects beads projects, finds active issue, sets OTEL env vars via CLAUDE_ENV_FILE. PostToolUse hook tracks mid-session issue switches via bd update commands. Both write to .beads/.session-map.jsonl for token attribution.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-qki","depends_on_id":"bw-co0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T16:20:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-qyd","title":"Spike: validate OTEL token tracking with Claude Code","description":"Quick spike to confirm OTEL telemetry export and/or ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL proxy actually capture token usage data from Claude Code. Success = we see real token counts attributed to an issue ID.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T15:22:36Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T15:59:21Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T15:59:21Z","close_reason":"Spike confirmed: OTEL telemetry export works out of the box. OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES passes custom issue_id through all metrics/events. No proxy needed.","labels":["spike"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-qyd","depends_on_id":"bw-co0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T15:22:40Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-co0","title":"Investigate tracking token usage per issue","description":"Explore whether there's a way to determine/track token consumption (LLM tokens) per beads issue. Could help with cost awareness, effort estimation, and understanding which issues are most expensive to work on.","notes":"## Final Checkpoint (2026-02-10)\nAll child tasks complete except bw-rx3 (blocked on story points). Investigation closed. Infrastructure: 3 global hooks, JSONL collector, API route, React Query hooks, dashboard UI. Commit 43bb76a.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T15:07:08Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:59:47Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T16:56:05Z","close_reason":"Token tracking investigation complete. All core tasks done: hooks (bw-qki), collector (bw-vnu), API (bw-dzj), dashboard UI (bw-fom). Only bw-rx3 (efficiency panel) remains, blocked on story points epic.","labels":["chore"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":5,"comment_count":0}
