{"id":"beads_web-fx2","title":"Review: PRODUCT_REPO_BASE not injectable in repo-path-resolver","description":"File: src/lib/repo-path-resolver.ts:27\n\nPRODUCT_REPO_BASE is a module-level constant ('/Users/janemckay/dev/claude_projects') that cannot be overridden via parameter or config. Unlike FLEET_CORE_PATH which is passed as a parameter to resolveRepoPath(), the product repo base is hardcoded.\n\nThis means:\n1. Tests cannot verify behavior with alternative base paths\n2. If the repo structure ever changes, two constants need updating (line 27 here + route.ts line 63 for FLEET_CORE_PATH)\n\nPer guardrails.md rule 9: 'If multiple files need the same path, consider a shared config rather than duplicating the constant.'\n\nAdditionally, FLEET_CORE_PATH is defined independently in both route.ts:63 and repo-path-resolver.ts:26.\n\nSuggested fix: Either make PRODUCT_REPO_BASE a parameter (like fleetCorePath already is) or extract both constants to a shared config module (e.g., src/lib/paths.ts).","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T12:15:42Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:21:05Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-l6q","title":"Review: Missing test for empty/blank epic title in sanitizeTopicName","description":"File: __tests__/lib/repo-path-resolver.test.ts\n\nThe sanitizeTopicName function has no test for edge cases:\n- Empty string input ('')\n- Whitespace-only input ('   ')\n- Title with only special characters ('!@#$%')\n\nThe function is called by resolveRepoPath for ventures and internal epics to construct filesystem paths. If it returns an empty string, the resulting research path would be something like fleet-core/docs/research/.md (a hidden file with no name), which would silently write to an unexpected location.\n\nAlso missing: no test for resolveRepoPath with unknown/unsupported ship type (e.g., 'banana'). The function currently falls through to the product ship type default, which may or may not be intentional. A test should document this behavior.\n\nSuggested fix: Add edge case tests for empty/blank input and verify the function handles them gracefully. Add a test for unknown ship type to document the fallback behavior.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T12:15:33Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:21:06Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-dex","title":"QA: Missing test coverage for send-for-qa, qa-fix-and-retest, and approve-and-build actions","notes":"**What's wrong:** The test file __tests__/api/fleet-action.test.ts has no test cases for three of the ten in-scope actions: send-for-qa, qa-fix-and-retest, and approve-and-build. The send-for-qa action has the most complex new logic in this epic (QA round detection at lines 501-504, platform-specific agent selection at lines 515-518). This logic is completely untested.\n\n**Root cause:** The test file covers 13 describe blocks but omits these three actions entirely.\n\n**Expected behavior:** Each action should have test coverage for: (1) correct label transitions, (2) correct agent launch parameters, (3) action-specific logic (QA round incrementing, platform QA agent selection, feature scope file reading for approve-and-build).\n\n**Suggested fix:** Add test describe blocks for: (1) send-for-qa -- test label transitions, QA round detection from existing qa:round-N labels, platform-specific agent selection (ios-app -\u003e platforms/ios/qa, web-app -\u003e qa), agentName is set. (2) qa-fix-and-retest -- test label transitions, no agentName set, pipelineStage is qa-fixes. (3) approve-and-build -- test label transitions, no agentName set, feature scope note handling.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T11:31:49Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T12:21:07Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-m8z","title":"Bug: Insights fails in __all__ mode — passes __all__ sentinel to Dolt reader","description":"getInsights (bv-client.ts:652) falls back to readIssuesFromDolt(resolvedPath) when bv fails. In __all__ mode, resolvedPath is the __all__ sentinel string, not a real repo path. readIssuesFromDolt throws 'No Dolt server port found for __all__'. Fix: getInsights needs to aggregate across repos in __all__ mode, same as getAllProjectsPlan does for issues.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:43:43Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:55:25Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:55:25Z","close_reason":"Fixed. Insights route now handles __all__ mode by aggregating issues from all repos via Promise.allSettled, then computing graph metrics on the combined set. Returns 2,528 issues with bottlenecks and keystones. 749/749 tests pass.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-nq9","title":"Update beads_web documentation for Dolt-only architecture","description":"19 markdown files in beads_web reference JSONL, SQLite, fallback chains, sqlite-reader, or jsonl-fallback. Key files: ARCHITECTURE.md (data layer description), CLAUDE.md (developer instructions), README.md (project overview), docs/API.md (API reference), docs/user-guide.md. These need updating to reflect the Dolt-only architecture. Also review: FACTORY_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md (may be entirely stale from gateway plan), fix-beads-fleet-split-brain-beads.md (may be stale), TASK*.md files (appear to be stale task tracking files that predate beads). Acceptance: all documentation reflects Dolt-only architecture, stale planning docs archived or deleted.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-13T01:27:22Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-13T01:35:31Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:35:31Z","close_reason":"Updated CLAUDE.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, and README.md for Dolt-only architecture. Replaced all SQLite/JSONL/fallback-chain references with Dolt reader descriptions. Updated data flow diagrams, module descriptions, file trees, tech stack tables, and deployment notes. Zero legacy references remaining in key docs.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"beads_web-6o5","title":"Add Langfuse tracing to beads-web application","description":"Instrument the Next.js dashboard with Langfuse observability. The app uses the Anthropic SDK directly for issue title cleanup (Claude Haiku). Add OpenTelemetry-based auto-instrumentation via @arizeai/openinference-instrumentation-anthropic and @langfuse/otel, with Next.js instrumentation.ts hook.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"Jane McKay","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-04-09T11:34:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-04-09T11:36:43Z","closed_at":"2026-04-09T11:36:43Z","close_reason":"Implemented Langfuse tracing with auto-instrumented Anthropic SDK via OpenTelemetry. Added src/lib/langfuse.ts, src/instrumentation.ts, updated next.config.mjs, .env.example, and wrapped the issue title cleanup API route.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
