{"id":"bw-a4w.6","title":"Label-based risk modifiers for estimates","description":"Phase 2: Create estimate-rules.ts with RISK_MODIFIERS map. Labels: external-api (+36h), architecture-change (+24h), ui-polish (+48h), needs-testing (+24h). Apply modifiers post-label-add. Backfill endpoint for existing beads.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:14Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:05:14Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T17:05:14Z","close_reason":"estimate-rules.ts with 7 risk modifiers, BASE_MINUTES, computeEstimate. Wired into estimateRelease.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.6","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:14Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-a4w.6","depends_on_id":"bw-a4w.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:58:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":3,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-gop","title":"Auto-compute complexity score when creating beads to improve release ETA accuracy","description":"Current release ETA uses priority as a proxy for effort, which is rough — priority reflects urgency, not complexity. Add a complexity calculation at bead creation time so estimates are based on actual expected effort. Questions to investigate: (1) What factors determine complexity? (description length, number of acceptance criteria, issue_type, dependency count, whether it touches multiple files/modules). (2) Should this be an AI-computed score (Haiku analysing the title+description) or rule-based (heuristic from structured fields)? (3) Where does the score live — the existing estimated_minutes column in the DB, a new complexity field, or a label like complexity:high? (4) How does this feed back into the release ETA — replace priority weights with complexity weights, or use both? (5) Should complexity be editable after creation? (6) Can we backfill complexity for existing beads from their descriptions? Goal: when a bead is created (via CLI or web quick-create), automatically assign a complexity/effort estimate that the release ETA calculation can use instead of relying solely on priority.","notes":"Architecture analysis complete. Recommended: Hybrid (Option E) in 4 phases. Full analysis at docs/complexity-estimation-architecture.md. Phase 1 (planner estimates) is the highest-value, lowest-effort starting point.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:48:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-24T09:54:54Z","closed_at":"2026-03-24T09:54:54Z","close_reason":"Haiku auto-estimates effort at bead creation time, feeds into release ETA pipeline","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-3cf","title":"Investigate: estimated time to completion per release based on bead complexity","description":"Request: Show an estimated time for completion for a release based on the cards in it. Investigate what level of complexity this involves. Questions to answer: (1) What signals exist in beads to estimate effort? (story_points, issue_type, priority, historical close rates from git timestamps). (2) Can we derive velocity from PatchCycle's 591 commits / 853 beads history? (3) What's the simplest useful estimate — e.g. count open beads * average days-per-bead from closed history? (4) Should estimates account for blocked/dependency chains? (5) Where does this display — on the release row, in the expanded view, or both? (6) Do we need a new API endpoint or can this be computed client-side from existing data? Deliverable: findings written to a file, with a recommendation on approach and complexity rating.","notes":"Full analysis at docs/release-eta-investigation.md","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-16T16:35:11Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-16T16:39:02Z","closed_at":"2026-03-16T16:39:02Z","close_reason":"Investigation complete. Recommended priority-weighted estimate using historical close times. Low-medium complexity, client-side only, no API changes. See docs/release-eta-investigation.md","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
