{"id":"bw-z5g","title":"Label autocomplete: suggest existing release:* labels when adding labels","description":"When adding a label to a bead in the UI, if the user types 'release:', show a dropdown of existing release:* labels from that project as suggestions. Prevents typos and inconsistency. Also applies to release-status:* labels. Related factory epic: cycle-apps-factory-nm1.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-08T15:47:30Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-09T00:00:51Z","closed_at":"2026-03-09T00:00:51Z","close_reason":"Label autocomplete with release:* and release-status:* suggestions on issue detail page","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-16f","title":"Mobile sidebar/project selector broken - cannot switch projects on phone","description":"On mobile (phone), the sidebar is inaccessible and users cannot select different projects. This blocks Jane from checking beads on her phone.\n\nP0 — this is her primary dashboard for tracking all work across projects.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Open beads-web on mobile phone\n2. Try to access sidebar / switch projects\n3. Sidebar does not appear or is not interactive\n\nNeeds investigation: is it a responsive CSS issue, a z-index problem, a missing hamburger menu, or a JS event handler not working on touch?","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-03-08T00:19:40Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:14Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:17:14Z","close_reason":"Done — RepoSelector now calls onSelect to close mobile drawer","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-bj1","title":"Add direct links to research report and plan from fleet cards","description":"Fleet cards and issue list should have quick-access links that jump directly to the research report and plan sections on the epic detail page (or open them in a new view). Currently you have to open the epic and scroll to find these sections. Add anchor links or dedicated buttons on fleet cards (e.g. small 'Research' and 'Plan' links) that navigate to /issue/\u003cid\u003e#research and /issue/\u003cid\u003e#plan. Requires adding id attributes to the Research and Plan section headers on the issue detail page.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-18T13:44:50Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-08T12:21:47Z","closed_at":"2026-03-08T12:21:47Z","close_reason":"Added anchor links and fleet card quick-access links","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-h5e","title":"Persist agent session to disk so hot-reload doesn't lose tracking","description":"Agent session state (activeSession, activeProcess) is held in-memory in agent-launcher.ts. When Next.js hot-reloads during development (e.g. editing agent-launcher.ts itself), the in-memory variables reset to null. The spawned agent process survives (detached, unref'd) but the dashboard loses tracking: banner disappears, Show Log stops working, and the exit handler that sets pipeline labels (e.g. plan:pending) never fires.\n\nFix: Write session metadata (pid, repoPath, epicId, pipelineStage, logFile, startedAt) to a JSON file on disk (e.g. /tmp/beads-web-agent-session.json). On getAgentStatus(), read from disk and verify the PID is still alive. On exit, clean up the file. This survives hot-reloads and even full server restarts.\n\nDiscovered when editing agent-launcher.ts to fix log formatting caused the running planner agent to become invisible to the dashboard.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-18T13:40:09Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-18T13:07:56Z","closed_at":"2026-03-18T13:07:56Z","close_reason":"Committed in 706bea3 — session persisted to temp JSON, recovered by PID check","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-48p","title":"Add submission agent launch from beads-web","description":"Approve Submission button calls POST /api/agent to prepare submission metadata, screenshots plan, keywords, description. Triggers the submission prep workflow defined in the factory CLAUDE.md. Agent runs in the app folder to access the built project.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:40:49Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","close_reason":"Submission agent launch implemented via fleet action API using sonnet model","labels":["agent-launch","pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-dbp","title":"Add Send back to Development button to Submission stage","description":"In the Submitted/Submission Prep column, add a Send back to Development button. Jane can write problems/feedback in a text field, confirm, and the issue re-enters In Development with her feedback added as a comment on the bead. This handles App Store rejections or issues Jane spots during review.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:40:37Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","close_reason":"Send back to Development button added to Submission Prep stage, removes submission-prep label and adds development label","labels":["pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-bxd","title":"Add Deprioritise button to Research Complete stage","description":"Add a Deprioritise button on fleet cards in the Research Complete column. Clicking it moves the issue to Bad Ideas column and closes it with a deprioritised label. This lets Jane quickly kill ideas that looked promising after research but aren't worth building.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-16T00:40:32Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T11:49:02Z","close_reason":"Deprioritise button added to Research Complete stage FleetCard, transitions to pipeline:bad-idea","labels":["pipeline"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-b2q","title":"Research report markdown reader from factory repo","description":"GET /api/research/[app-name] reads markdown reports from factory repo apps/\u003capp-name\u003e/research/report.md. Markdown rendering on issue detail page for research-labeled issues.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:59:09Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T21:07:54Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T21:07:54Z","close_reason":"Research report markdown reader: GET /api/research/[appName], react-markdown rendering with GFM, integrated on issue detail page for research-labeled issues. 7 new tests, 515 total passing.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-37k","title":"Factory workflow buttons: Approve \u0026 Request More Research","description":"Add factory-specific workflow buttons to issue detail page: 'Approve \u0026 Send to Development' closes research task with approval reason, 'Request More Research' adds comment. Shows when issue has research label.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:54:24Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T20:59:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T20:59:02Z","close_reason":"Factory workflow buttons: Approve \u0026 Send to Development, Request More Research (comment action), on both detail page and kanban panel. 3 new tests, 508 total passing.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-mr5","title":"Agent Activity Timeline","description":"Show when agents started/stopped work on issues. Visualize session durations, token usage, and task completion. Timeline view on fleet page and issue detail page.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:39:27Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T20:46:23Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T20:46:23Z","close_reason":"Agent Activity Timeline implemented: visual timeline with day groups, color-coded session bars, tooltips, summary stats. Added to fleet page and issue detail page. 73 tests, build clean.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-qzv","title":"Auto-Registration — detect new beads projects and register with dashboard","description":"When factory creates a new app project with .beads/, auto-register it with the dashboard. Watch for new projects or provide a simple registration mechanism. From factory integration plan item 4.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:29:28Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T20:37:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T20:37:15Z","close_reason":"Auto-registration via watch directories: settings UI for managing watch dirs, auto-scan on page load, manual scan button, POST /api/repos scan+set-watch-dirs actions. 3 new tests.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-we4","title":"Research Completion Signals — webhook/polling API for factory agent","description":"When research tasks close, provide a way for the factory agent to detect it. Add a polling endpoint that returns recently closed issues with label filters, so the factory agent can check for completed research and prompt Jane for review.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:23:05Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T20:29:05Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T20:29:05Z","close_reason":"Signals polling API implemented: GET /api/signals?since=\u003cts\u003e\u0026label=\u003clabel\u003e returns recently closed issues. Factory agent can poll to detect research completion. 13 new tests.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-ag8","title":"Cost Per App Metric — aggregate token usage by epic","description":"Aggregate token usage by epic to show per-app costs. Show total cost, cost by phase (research/dev/submission), on fleet cards and issue detail. From factory integration plan item 2.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:17:26Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T20:22:38Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T20:22:38Z","close_reason":"Cost-per-app metric implemented: fleet cards show per-epic cost + phase breakdown, issue detail shows App Cost section with phase bars, fleet header shows total fleet cost. 10 new tests.","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-aim","title":"App Fleet Dashboard View","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T20:06:15Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T20:14:37Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T20:14:37Z","close_reason":"Fleet dashboard implemented: /fleet page with pipeline kanban (Idea/Research/Development/Submission/Completed), stage detection from children labels, 37 new tests, sidebar nav + keyboard shortcut","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-270","title":"Factory: Add workflow action buttons","description":"Add write/mutation capabilities to the dashboard. Key actions: 'Approve \u0026 send to development' button, status change buttons, 'Request more research' button. Currently beads_web is read-only. These buttons would call bd CLI commands to update issue status.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T00:38:05Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T11:15:07Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T11:15:07Z","close_reason":"Implemented workflow action buttons: API route, mutation hook, buttons on issue detail page and kanban panel, ARCHITECTURE.md updated","labels":["factory-integration"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-ctu","title":"Factory: Add research report storage and display","description":"Store and display research reports (market analysis, competitor analysis, product research) for each app build. Reports could be stored in issue descriptions or a new dedicated field. Factory agent produces these during research phase.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-15T00:37:55Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-15T19:42:40Z","closed_at":"2026-02-15T19:42:40Z","close_reason":"Implemented: notes display, epic progress bars, submission tracking with colored badges and Submissions built-in view","labels":["factory-integration"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-cg1","title":"Show what epics an issue is part of in the dashboard","description":"Display parent epic(s) for each issue in the beads_web dashboard. Show epic membership in the issue table and/or issue detail page, so users can see which epic(s) an issue belongs to.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-14T13:35:04Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-14T13:41:36Z","closed_at":"2026-02-14T13:41:36Z","close_reason":"Added story_points + epic fields to data model, epic column with filtering in dashboard","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-1mx","title":"Build tokens-per-story-point efficiency panel","description":"Build the efficiency metrics panel for the dashboard: tokens_per_story_point, cost_per_story_point computed metrics, scatter chart of tokens vs story points across issues. This is the final deliverable of bw-rx3. Depends on story_points being in the web data model and the OTEL collector properly attributing tokens to issues.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T17:55:43Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-03-24T10:03:05Z","closed_at":"2026-03-24T10:03:05Z","close_reason":"Efficiency panel already implemented in commit 157b37d with tokens_per_sp, cost_per_sp metrics, summary cards, and bar chart visualization","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-1mx","depends_on_id":"bw-91h","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T17:55:47Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-1mx","depends_on_id":"bw-xsq","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T17:55:47Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-5g0","title":"Add story_points to BeadsIssue/PlanIssue types and JSONL parser","description":"The CLI now exports story_points in JSONL but the web dashboard doesn't consume it. Add story_points field to BeadsIssue and PlanIssue interfaces in src/lib/types.ts, and update the JSONL parser to read it.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T17:55:37Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-14T13:41:36Z","closed_at":"2026-02-14T13:41:36Z","close_reason":"Added story_points + epic fields to data model, epic column with filtering in dashboard","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-w15","title":"Include story points in bd export/import JSONL format","description":"Ensure story points are included in the JSONL export format and properly imported. Update the export and import commands to handle the story_points field for data portability.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:44Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","close_reason":"Implemented story_points across 19 files in beads CLI repo on feature/story-points branch","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-w15","depends_on_id":"bw-6gw","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:49Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-w15","depends_on_id":"bw-wpz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:54Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-5io","title":"Add story points to bd stats reporting","description":"Integrate story points into bd stats output. Show total points open, total points closed, points by status, and optionally velocity (points closed per time period). Useful for sprint planning and progress tracking.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:42Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","close_reason":"Implemented story_points across 19 files in beads CLI repo on feature/story-points branch","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-5io","depends_on_id":"bw-6gw","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:49Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-5io","depends_on_id":"bw-wpz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:54Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-b8y","title":"Display story points in bd list, show, and ready output","description":"Show story points in the output of bd list, bd show, and bd ready commands. Include points column in list/ready table output and a points field in show detail output. Handle nil/unset gracefully (show dash or omit).","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:41Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","close_reason":"Implemented story_points across 19 files in beads CLI repo on feature/story-points branch","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-b8y","depends_on_id":"bw-6gw","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:48Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-b8y","depends_on_id":"bw-8pl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:54Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-b8y","depends_on_id":"bw-wpz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:53Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":3,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-8pl","title":"Add --points flag to bd create and bd update CLI","description":"Add a --points flag to the bd create and bd update commands so users can set story points when creating or updating issues. Accept integer values. Validate that points are non-negative.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:38Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","close_reason":"Implemented story_points across 19 files in beads CLI repo on feature/story-points branch","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-8pl","depends_on_id":"bw-6gw","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:48Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"},{"issue_id":"bw-8pl","depends_on_id":"bw-wpz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:53Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":2,"dependent_count":1,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-wpz","title":"Add story_points field to issue schema","description":"Add a story_points integer field to the beads issue data model. Update the database schema (SQLite + JSONL serialization) to support storing point values on issues. Points should be nullable (not all issues need estimates).","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:37Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:15Z","close_reason":"Implemented story_points across 19 files in beads CLI repo on feature/story-points branch","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"bw-wpz","depends_on_id":"bw-6gw","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:18:47Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":4,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-6gw","title":"Add story points capture to beads issues","description":"Epic: Add the ability to capture and track story points on beads issues. Story points provide a relative estimate of effort/complexity for planning and velocity tracking. This includes schema changes, CLI support for setting/displaying points, and integration with stats/reporting.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-10T14:17:35Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:19Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T17:48:19Z","close_reason":"Story points epic complete: schema, CLI flags, display, stats, export/import all implemented across 19 files","labels":["epic"],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":6,"comment_count":0}
{"id":"bw-6jq","title":"Dashboard should refresh data at a sensible interval without jarring the UI","description":"Currently the dashboard data may go stale or refresh too aggressively. Implement smooth polling with React Query that updates data at a reasonable interval (e.g. 30s) without causing layout shifts, flickering, or losing scroll position. The refresh should be invisible to the user unless new data actually changes what's displayed.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"janemckay@me.com","created_at":"2026-02-09T01:40:32Z","created_by":"Jane McKay","updated_at":"2026-02-09T01:45:32Z","closed_at":"2026-02-09T01:45:32Z","close_reason":"Added tiered polling (30s issues, 60s metrics, none for static data) with keepPreviousData to prevent UI jarring","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
